[ERR] 2026-01-23 02:18:04 | INFO | Tool Bash called with {'command': "cat > /tmp/LIGHTST_ANALYSIS.md << 'EOF'\n# LightST Repository Analysis\n## Efficient Traffic Prediction through Spatio-Temporal Distillation\n\n**Repository URL**: https://github.com/lizzyhku/TP  \n**Cloned to**: /home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST  \n**Conference**: AAAI 2025  \n**Published**: Zhang et al., 2025\n\n---\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nLightST is an efficient traffic prediction model that uses spatio-temporal knowledge distillation to train a lightweight student network (STMLP) with guidance from a more complex teacher network (Teacher/MTGNN-based). The model is designed for traffic flow prediction on multi-sensor datasets like PeMSD4, PeMSD8, and PeMSBay.\n\n### Key Characteristics:\n- **Task**: Traffic flow prediction (time-series forecasting)\n- **Input**: 12 time steps of historical traffic flow (1 hour)\n- **Output**: 12 future time steps of predicted traffic flow (1 hour)\n- **Framework**: PyTorch\n- **Python Version**: 3.9.13\n- **PyTorch Version**: 1.12.1\n\n---\n\n## Repository Structure\n\n```\nrepos/LightST/\n├── model/                          # Model implementations\n│   ├── Teacher.py                  # Teacher model (complex) & Student model (STMLP)\n│   ├── Mains.py                    # Main training entry point\n│   ├── BasicTrainer.py             # Training loop and distillation logic\n│   ├── PEMS04_MTGNN.conf          # Configuration for PEMS04 dataset\n│   ├── PEMS03_MTGNN.conf          # Configuration for PEMS03 dataset\n│   ├── PEMS08_MTGNN.conf          # Configuration for PEMS08 dataset\n│   ├── SAVE/                       # Directory for saved model checkpoints\n│   └── init.py\n├── lib/                            # Utility libraries\n│   ├── dataloader.py               # Data loading and preprocessing\n│   ├── load_dataset.py             # Dataset loading from NPZ files\n│   ├── metrics.py                  # Evaluation metrics (MAE, RMSE, MAPE)\n│   ├── normalization.py            # Data normalization strategies\n│   ├── TrainInits.py               # Training initialization utilities\n│   ├── pre_graph.py                # Adjacency matrix generation\n│   ├── add_window.py               # Sliding window generation\n│   ├── logger.py                   # Logging utilities\n│   └── init.py\n├── PEMS_data/                      # Data directory (not included in clone)\n│   └── <dataset_name>/\n│       ├── <dataset>.npz           # Traffic flow data\n│       ├── <dataset>.csv           # Distance matrix\n│       └── <dataset>.txt           # Optional node IDs\n└── README.md                       # Documentation\n\n```\n\n---\n\n## Key Model Files and Classes\n\n### 1. **Teacher.py** (/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST/model/Teacher.py)\n\n#### Main Classes:\n- **Teacher (lines 337-546)**: Complex teacher model with full architecture\n  - Input: (batch_size, seq_len, num_nodes, feature_dim)\n  - Output: (batch_size, output_window, num_nodes, 1)\n  - Returns 3 outputs: prediction, temporal_attention (ttout), spatial_attention (ssout)\n  \n- **STMLP (lines 547-747)**: Student model - Lightweight version with MLP-only architecture\n  - Simplified architecture compared to Teacher\n  - Uses sequential MLP layers instead of full GCN\n  - 3 MLP blocks for progressive spatial-temporal processing\n  - Returns 3 outputs: main prediction, distillation features (x_), and intermediate features (x)\n\n#### Key Components in Both Models:\n- **DilatedInception**: Temporal convolution blocks with dilated kernels\n- **GraphConstructor**: Learns adaptive spatial adjacency matrix\n- **MixProp**: Mixed-scale propagation for graph convolution\n- **LayerNorm**: Custom layer normalization\n- **Transformer Encoder**: Self-attention mechanism (optional, partially used)\n\n#### Architecture Details:\n```python\n# Dilation-based temporal convolution\n- Kernel sizes: [2, 3, 6, 7]\n- Dilation factor: configurable (default: 1)\n- Layers: 3 (configurable)\n\n# GCN (Graph Convolutional Network)\n- GCN depth: 2\n- Propagation alpha: 0.05\n- Subgraph size: 20 nodes\n- Node embedding dim: 40\n\n# Channels\n- Residual channels: 32\n- Conv channels: 32\n- Skip channels: 64\n- End channels: 128\n\n# Attention\n- d_model: 12\n- nheads: 4\n- num_layers: 3\n```\n\n### 2. **Mains.py** (/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST/model/Mains.py)\n\n#### Purpose: Main training entry point\n\n#### Key Components:\n- **Command-line arguments parsing**: Dataset, device, model, data/train parameters\n- **Configuration loading**: From .conf files\n- **Model initialization**: Creates STMLP student network\n- **Data loading**: Uses get_dataloader for train/val/test splits\n- **Loss functions**: mask_mae, mae, mse\n- **Optimizer**: Adam with learning rate decay\n- **Training execution**: Via Trainer.trainS() method\n\n#### Key Parameters:\n```python\n# Data\ndataset: 'PEMS04' (configurable to PEMS08, PEMS03, PEMS07, PeMSBAY)\nlag: 12 (input window)\nhorizon: 12 (output window)\nnum_nodes: 307 (varies by dataset)\n\n# Training\nbatch_size: 32 (PEMS04/08/03), 64 (PEMS07)\nepochs: 100\nlearning_rate: 0.003\ndropout: 0.3\nearly_stopping: True (patience=15)\n\n# Loss\nPrimary loss: MAE (mask_mae with scaler normalization)\nDistillation loss: KL divergence (weight=10)\nContrastive losses: Spatial-temporal contrastive (weight=1)\n```\n\n### 3. **BasicTrainer.py** (/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST/model/BasicTrainer.py)\n\n#### Purpose: Training loop with knowledge distillation\n\n#### Key Methods:\n\n**trainS() (lines 267-337+)**: \n- Main student training method with teacher distillation\n- Calls train_epochs() for each epoch\n\n**train_epochs() (lines 149-205)**:\n- One epoch of student training with teacher guidance\n- Loss computation:\n  ```\n  loss = MAE_loss(student_output, target) \n       + 10 * KL_divergence(student, teacher)\n       + 1 * spatial_temporal_contrastive_loss\n  ```\n- Gradient clipping and optimization\n\n**val_epoch() (lines 57-74)**:\n- Validation without teacher guidance\n- Returns MAE loss on validation set\n\n**loss_cls(), loss_clt() (lines 109-147)**:\n- Spatial-temporal contrastive losses\n- Measure similarity between student and teacher intermediate features\n- Temperature-scaled cosine similarity\n\n#### Teacher Loading:\n```python\n# Teacher model initialized and loaded from pre-trained checkpoint\nloadTeacher(args):\n  tmodel = Teacher(args)\n  tmodel.load_state_dict(torch.load('./SAVE/PEMS04/best_model.pth'))\n  return tmodel\n```\n\n### 4. **dataloader.py** (/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST/lib/dataloader.py)\n\n#### Functions:\n- **get_dataloader()**: Main data loading function\n- **normalize_dataset()**: Applies normalization (std, max01, max11, etc.)\n- **split_data_by_ratio()**: Train/val/test split\n- **data_loader()**: PyTorch DataLoader creation\n\n#### Data Processing Pipeline:\n1. Load raw dataset (NPZ files)\n2. Add temporal features (day-of-week, time-of-day)\n3. Normalize data (default: standard normalization)\n4. Split into train/val/test\n5. Create sliding windows (lag=12, horizon=12)\n6. Normalize each split separately with scaler\n\n#### Output Format:\n- **X**: (num_samples, seq_len, num_nodes, 3)\n  - 3 channels: traffic_flow, day_feature, week_feature\n- **Y**: (num_samples, forecast_len, num_nodes, 3)\n\n### 5. **load_dataset.py** (/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST/lib/load_dataset.py)\n\n#### Supported Datasets:\n- **PEMS04**: 307 nodes\n- **PEMS08**: 170 nodes  \n- **PEMS03**: 358 nodes\n- **PEMS07**: 883 nodes\n- **PeMSBAY**: 325 nodes (mentioned in README)\n\n#### Data Loading:\n- Reads NPZ files: `<dataset>.npz`\n- Extracts traffic flow (first channel)\n- Generates temporal features:\n  - Day-of-day index (0-287 for 5-min intervals)\n  - Week-of-week index (0-7)\n- Output shape: (timestamps, num_nodes, 3_channels)\n\n### 6. **metrics.py** (/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST/lib/metrics.py)\n\n#### Evaluation Metrics:\n- **MAE** (Mean Absolute Error)\n- **MSE** (Mean Squared Error)\n- **RMSE** (Root Mean Squared Error)\n- **RRSE** (Relative Root Squared Error)\n- **CORR** (Correlation)\n- **MAPE** (Mean Absolute Percentage Error)\n\n#### Features:\n- Mask-based filtering (removes zero/invalid values)\n- Torch-based computation for GPU acceleration\n\n### 7. **pre_graph.py** (/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST/lib/pre_graph.py)\n\n#### Purpose:\n- Computes adjacency matrix from distance matrix\n- Distance-based graph construction\n- Inverse distance weighting\n\n---\n\n## Configuration Files\n\n### Example: PEMS04_MTGNN.conf\n\n```ini\n[data]\nnum_nodes = 307\nlag = 12\nhorizon = 12\nval_ratio = 0.2\ntest_ratio = 0.2\ntod = False\nnormalizer = std\ncolumn_wise = False\ndefault_graph = True\n\n[model]\ninput_dim = 1\noutput_dim = 1\ninput_window = 12\noutput_window = 12\n\ngcn_true = True\nbuildA_true = True\ngcn_depth = 2\ndropout = 0.3\nsubgraph_size = 20\nnode_dim = 40\ndilation_exponential = 1\nconv_channels = 32\nresidual_channels = 32\nskip_channels = 64\nend_channels = 128\nlayers = 3\npropalpha = 0.05\ntanhalpha = 3\nlayer_norm_affline = True\nuse_curriculum_learning = True\ntask_level = 0\n\n[train]\nloss_func = mask_mae\nseed = 52\nbatch_size = 32\nepochs = 100\nlr_init = 0.003\nlr_decay = True\nlr_decay_rate = 0.3\nlr_decay_step = 25,45,60,75\nearly_stop = True\nearly_stop_patience = 15\ngrad_norm = True\nmax_grad_norm = 5\nreal_value = False\n\n[test]\nmae_thresh = None\nmape_thresh = 0.\n\n[log]\nlog_step = 20\nplot = False\n```\n\n---\n\n## Dependencies and Requirements\n\n### Python Version\n- Python 3.9.13\n\n### Core Framework\n- PyTorch 1.12.1\n\n### Key Imports Used:\n```python\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn as nn\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\nimport numpy as np\nimport configparser  # Config file parsing\nimport argparse      # CLI arguments\n```\n\n### No External Package Dependencies Explicit:\n- The code uses only PyTorch and NumPy\n- No special requirements.txt file found\n\n---\n\n## Data Format Expectations\n\n### Input Data Format:\n1. **Traffic Flow Data (NPZ files)**:\n   - Shape: (num_timestamps, num_nodes, 1)\n   - Values: Traffic flow counts (vehicles per time interval)\n   - Format: numpy compressed archive (.npz)\n\n2. **Graph Structure**:\n   - CSV file with distance matrix\n   - Optional TXT file with node IDs\n   - Distance-based adjacency construction\n\n3. **Time Window**:\n   - Input: 12 consecutive 5-minute intervals (1 hour)\n   - Output: Predict next 12 intervals (1 hour)\n   - Training: Using 80% data, Validation: 10%, Test: 10%\n\n### Data Normalization:\n- **Standard Normalization** (default):\n  - Per-channel mean and std computed from training data\n  - Applied to train/val/test separately\n  - Inverse transformation for loss calculation\n\n---\n\n## Training Pipeline\n\n### Step 1: Data Preparation\n```\nRaw NPZ → Normalize → Split (80-10-10) → Add windows (lag=12, horizon=12)\n```\n\n### Step 2: Model Initialization\n```\nInitialize STMLP (student model with MLP layers)\nLoad pre-trained Teacher model checkpoint\n```\n\n### Step 3: Training Loop (trainS method)\n```\nFor each epoch:\n  1. Student forward pass: (X) → student_output, distill_features\n  2. Teacher forward pass: (X) → teacher_output, teacher_features\n  3. Compute losses:\n     - MAE(student_output, target)\n     - KL_divergence(student, teacher) * 10\n     - Spatial-temporal_contrastive_loss * 1\n  4. Backward pass + gradient clipping\n  5. Validation on val set\n  6. Early stopping if no improvement for 15 epochs\n```\n\n### Step 4: Model Checkpointing\n- Best model saved to: `./SAVE/<DATASET>/best_modelstudent.pth`\n- Test evaluation on held-out test set\n\n---\n\n## Running the Code\n\n### Command Format:\n```bash\npython Mains.py --data <DATASET>\n```\n\n### Supported Datasets:\n```bash\npython Mains.py --data PEMS04   # 307 nodes\npython Mains.py --data PEMS08   # 170 nodes\npython Mains.py --data PEMS03   # 358 nodes\npython Mains.py --data PEMS07   # 883 nodes\npython Mains.py --data PeMSBAY  # 325 nodes\n```\n\n### Expected Output:\n- Training logs to console\n- Model checkpoint: `./model/SAVE/<DATASET>/best_modelstudent.pth`\n- Test metrics: MAE, RMSE, MAPE\n\n---\n\n## Key Architectural Innovations\n\n### 1. **Student-Teacher Distillation**:\n- Teacher: Full MTGNN-based model with GCN\n- Student: Lightweight STMLP with only MLP layers\n- Distillation weight: 10x KL divergence loss\n\n### 2. **Spatio-Temporal Contrastive Learning**:\n- Contrastive loss between student and teacher features\n- Separate spatial and temporal contrastive losses\n- Temperature: 0.05\n\n### 3. **Multi-Level Representation**:\n- Temporal features from dilated convolutions\n- Spatial propagation via MixProp\n- Attention-based feature aggregation (optional)\n\n### 4. **Efficiency Metrics**:\n- Student model uses only MLP instead of GCN\n- Significant parameter reduction vs. Teacher\n- Maintains performance through distillation\n\n---\n\n## Notable Implementation Details\n\n### 1. **Graph Construction**:\n- Dynamic adjacency matrix learning via GraphConstructor\n- Top-k sparsification (k=20)\n- Pre-defined adjacency option\n\n### 2. **Receptive Field Calculation**:\n```python\nreceptive_field = layers * (kernel_size - 1) + output_dim\n# With kernel_size=7, layers=3: RF = 3 * 6 + 12 = 30\n```\n\n### 3. **Input Padding**:\n- Automatic padding if input_window < receptive_field\n- Maintains temporal consistency\n\n### 4. **Learning Rate Schedule**:\n- Initial LR: 0.003\n- Decay at epochs: 25, 45, 60, 75\n- Decay rate: 0.3\n\n### 5. **Gradient Clipping**:\n- Max gradient norm: 5\n- Prevents training instability\n\n---\n\n## Data Availability\n\nThe paper mentions:\n- Training datasets available on Google Drive\n- Link: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/146BOfs03ljP1OrWnVzdoleuywzCTpS69?usp=sharing\n- Includes: PEMS04, PEMS08, PEMS03, PEMS07, PeMSBAY\n\n---\n\n## Paper Citation\n\n```bibtex\n@inproceedings{zhang2025efficient,\n  title={Efficient traffic prediction through spatio-temporal distillation},\n  author={Zhang, Qianru and Gao, Xinyi and Wang, Haixin and Yiu, Siu Ming and Yin, Hongzhi},\n  booktitle={Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence},\n  volume={39},\n  number={1},\n  pages={1093--1101},\n  year={2025}\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Migration Considerations for LibCity\n\n### Strengths:\n1. Clear separation of teacher/student models\n2. Well-documented data loading pipeline\n3. Standard PyTorch components\n4. Clean configuration system\n\n### Challenges:\n1. Teacher model must be pre-trained and loaded during student training\n2. Knowledge distillation loss requires careful tuning\n3. Contrastive loss functions are custom implementations\n4. Graph construction requires adjacency matrix input\n\n### Key Files to Integrate:\n- **Model**: STMLP class from Teacher.py (lightweight student)\n- **Trainer**: Knowledge distillation logic from BasicTrainer.trainS()\n- **Data**: Dataloader pipeline from dataloader.py\n- **Utils**: Metrics and normalization from lib/\n\n### Configuration Parameters to Expose:\n- Distillation weight (KL loss coefficient)\n- Contrastive loss weight\n- Temperature for contrastive learning\n- Teacher model checkpoint path\n- Graph construction parameters\n\nEOF\ncat /tmp/LIGHTST_ANALYSIS.md\n", 'description': 'Create comprehensive LightST analysis report'}
