[ERR] 2026-01-23 02:19:02 | INFO | Tool Bash called with {'command': 'cat > /home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/LIGHTST_CODE_SNIPPETS.md << \'EOF\'\n# LightST - Key Code Snippets and Implementation Details\n\n## 1. Student Model Architecture (STMLP)\n\n### Class Definition\n**File**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST/model/Teacher.py` (lines 547-747)\n\n```python\nclass STMLP(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, args):\n        super(STMLP, self).__init__()\n        \n        self.adj_mx = args.adj_mx\n        self.num_nodes = args.num_nodes\n        self.feature_dim = args.input_dim\n        self.input_window = args.input_window\n        self.output_window = args.output_window\n        self.output_dim = args.output_dim\n        self.device = args.device\n        \n        # Dilated temporal convolutions\n        self.filter_convs = nn.ModuleList()\n        self.gate_convs = nn.ModuleList()\n        self.skip_convs = nn.ModuleList()\n        \n        # MLP layers for lightweight spatial processing\n        self.stu_mlp = nn.ModuleList()\n        self.stu_mlp.append(nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(13,13),nn.Linear(13,13),nn.Linear(13,13)))\n        self.stu_mlp.append(nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(7,7),nn.Linear(7,7),nn.Linear(7,7)))\n        self.stu_mlp.append(nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(1,1),nn.Linear(1,1),nn.Linear(1,1)))\n        \n        # Start convolution\n        self.start_conv = nn.Conv2d(in_channels=self.feature_dim,\n                                    out_channels=self.residual_channels,\n                                    kernel_size=(1, 1))\n        \n        # End convolution\n        self.end_conv_1 = nn.Conv2d(in_channels=self.skip_channels,\n                                    out_channels=self.end_channels, kernel_size=(1, 1), bias=True)\n        self.end_conv_2 = nn.Conv2d(in_channels=self.end_channels,\n                                    out_channels=self.output_window, kernel_size=(1, 1), bias=True)\n    \n    def forward(self, source, idx=None):\n        inputs = source.transpose(1, 3)  # (batch, feature_dim, num_nodes, input_window)\n        \n        # Input padding if needed\n        if self.input_window < self.receptive_field:\n            inputs = nn.functional.pad(inputs, (self.receptive_field-self.input_window, 0, 0, 0))\n        \n        # Initial convolution\n        x = self.start_conv(inputs)\n        skip = self.skip0(F.dropout(inputs, self.dropout, training=self.training))\n        \n        # Temporal convolution with MLP spatial processing\n        for i in range(self.layers):\n            residual = x\n            filters = self.filter_convs[i](x)\n            filters = torch.tanh(filters)\n            gate = self.gate_convs[i](x)\n            gate = torch.sigmoid(gate)\n            x = filters * gate\n            x = F.dropout(x, self.dropout, training=self.training)\n            \n            s = x\n            s = self.skip_convs[i](s)\n            skip = s + skip\n            \n            # MLP layer replaces GCN in student\n            x = self.stu_mlp[i](x)\n            x = x + residual[:, :, :, -x.size(3):]\n            x = self.norm[i](x, self.idx)\n        \n        # Final layers\n        skip = self.skipE(x) + skip\n        x = F.relu(skip)\n        x = F.relu(self.end_conv_1(x))\n        x = self.end_conv_2(x)\n        x_ = nn.Linear(1, 32).cuda()(x)\n        \n        return x, x_, x  # main_pred, distill_features, intermediate\n```\n\n## 2. Teacher Model\n\n**File**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST/model/Teacher.py` (lines 337-546)\n\n```python\nclass Teacher(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, args):\n        super(Teacher, self).__init__()\n        \n        # Similar initialization to STMLP\n        self.adj_mx = args.adj_mx\n        self.num_nodes = args.num_nodes\n        \n        # Key difference: Uses GCN for spatial processing\n        self.gconv1 = nn.ModuleList()\n        self.gconv2 = nn.ModuleList()\n        \n        # Graph constructor for dynamic adjacency\n        self.gc = GraphConstructor(self.num_nodes, self.subgraph_size, \n                                   self.node_dim, self.device, \n                                   alpha=self.tanhalpha, \n                                   static_feat=self.static_feat)\n    \n    def forward(self, source, idx=None):\n        sout = []\n        tout = []\n        inputs = source.transpose(1, 3)\n        \n        if self.input_window < self.receptive_field:\n            inputs = nn.functional.pad(inputs, (self.receptive_field-self.input_window, 0, 0, 0))\n        \n        # Get adaptive adjacency matrix\n        if self.gcn_true:\n            if self.buildA_true:\n                if idx is None:\n                    adp = self.gc(self.idx)\n                else:\n                    adp = self.gc(idx)\n            else:\n                adp = self.predefined_A\n        \n        x = self.start_conv(inputs)\n        skip = self.skip0(F.dropout(inputs, self.dropout, training=self.training))\n        \n        # Temporal convolution with GCN spatial processing\n        for i in range(self.layers):\n            residual = x\n            filters = self.filter_convs[i](x)\n            filters = torch.tanh(filters)\n            gate = self.gate_convs[i](x)\n            gate = torch.sigmoid(gate)\n            x = filters * gate\n            x = F.dropout(x, self.dropout, training=self.training)\n            tout.append(x)\n            \n            s = x\n            s = self.skip_convs[i](s)\n            skip = s + skip\n            \n            if self.gcn_true:\n                # GCN for spatial processing\n                x = self.gconv1[i](x, adp) + self.gconv2[i](x, adp.transpose(1, 0))\n            \n            x = x + residual[:, :, :, -x.size(3):]\n            x = self.norm[i](x, self.idx)\n            sout.append(x)\n        \n        skip = self.skipE(x) + skip\n        x = F.relu(skip)\n        x = F.relu(self.end_conv_1(x))\n        x = self.end_conv_2(x)\n        \n        # Teacher returns 3 outputs for distillation\n        ttout = nn.Linear(1, 32).cuda()(nn.Linear(self.residual_channels, self.input_window)\n                                        .cuda()(tout[-1].transpose(1,3)).transpose(1,3))\n        ssout = nn.Linear(1, 32).cuda()(nn.Linear(self.residual_channels, self.input_window)\n                                        .cuda()(sout[-1].transpose(1,3)).transpose(1,3))\n        \n        return x, ttout, ssout  # main_pred, temporal_features, spatial_features\n```\n\n## 3. Knowledge Distillation Training\n\n**File**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST/model/BasicTrainer.py` (lines 149-205)\n\n```python\ndef train_epochs(self, epoch):\n    self.tmodel.eval()  # Teacher in eval mode\n    self.model.train()  # Student in train mode\n    total_loss = 0\n    \n    for batch_idx, (data, target) in enumerate(self.train_loader):\n        data = data[..., :self.args.input_dim]\n        label = target[..., :self.args.output_dim]\n        \n        self.optimizer.zero_grad()\n        \n        # Student forward pass\n        out, out_, _ = self.model(data)\n        \n        # Teacher forward pass (no grad)\n        with torch.no_grad():\n            gout, tout, sout = self.tmodel(data)\n        \n        if self.args.real_value:\n            label = self.scaler.inverse_transform(label)\n        \n        # 1. Main prediction loss (MAE)\n        loss1 = self.loss(out.cuda(), label)\n        \n        # 2. Temporal contrastive loss\n        tcl = self.loss_clt(out_, tout)\n        \n        # 3. Spatial contrastive loss\n        scl = self.loss_cls(out_, sout)\n        \n        # 4. KL divergence loss\n        kl_loss = nn.KLDivLoss(reduction="batchmean", log_target=True).cuda()\n        gout = F.log_softmax(gout).cuda()\n        mlp_emb_ = F.log_softmax(out).cuda()\n        tkloss = kl_loss(mlp_emb_.cuda().float(), gout.cuda().float())\n        \n        # Combined loss with weights\n        loss = loss1 + 10*tkloss + 1*scl\n        \n        loss.backward()\n        \n        # Gradient clipping\n        if self.args.grad_norm:\n            torch.nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_(self.model.parameters(), self.args.max_grad_norm)\n        \n        self.optimizer.step()\n        total_loss += loss.item()\n        \n        if batch_idx % self.args.log_step == 0:\n            self.logger.info(\'Train Epoch {}: {}/{} Loss: {:.6f}\'.format(\n                epoch, batch_idx, self.train_per_epoch, loss.item()))\n    \n    train_epoch_loss = total_loss / self.train_per_epoch\n    return train_epoch_loss\n```\n\n## 4. Contrastive Loss Functions\n\n**File**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST/model/BasicTrainer.py` (lines 109-147)\n\n```python\ndef loss_cls(self, x1, x2):\n    """Spatial contrastive loss"""\n    temperature = 0.05\n    x1 = F.normalize(x1, p=2, dim=-1)\n    x2 = F.normalize(x2, p=2, dim=-1)\n    weight = F.cosine_similarity(x1, x2, dim=-1)\n    \n    batch_size = x1.size()[0]\n    out = torch.cat([x1, x2], dim=0)\n    neg = torch.exp(torch.matmul(out, out.transpose(2,3).contiguous()) / temperature)\n    \n    pos = torch.exp(torch.sum(x1 * x2, dim=-1)*weight / temperature)\n    pos = torch.cat([pos, pos], dim=0).sum(dim=1)\n    \n    Ng = neg.sum(dim=-1).sum(dim=1)\n    loss = (- torch.log(pos / (pos + Ng))).mean()\n    \n    return loss\n\ndef loss_clt(self, x1, x2):\n    """Temporal contrastive loss"""\n    temperature = 0.05\n    x1 = F.normalize(x1, p=2, dim=-1)\n    x2 = F.normalize(x2, p=2, dim=-1)\n    weight = F.cosine_similarity(x1, x2, dim=-1)\n    \n    batch_size = x1.size()[0]\n    out = torch.cat([x1, x2], dim=0)\n    neg = torch.exp(torch.matmul(out, out.transpose(2,3).contiguous()) / temperature)\n    \n    pos = torch.exp(torch.sum(x1 * x2, dim=-1)*weight / temperature)\n    pos = torch.cat([pos, pos], dim=0).sum(dim=-1)\n    \n    Ng = neg.sum(dim=-1).sum(dim=-1)\n    loss = (- torch.log(pos / (pos + Ng))).mean()\n    \n    return loss\n```\n\n## 5. Data Loading Pipeline\n\n**File**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST/lib/dataloader.py` (lines 101-159)\n\n```python\ndef get_dataloader(args, normalizer=\'std\', tod=False, dow=False, weather=False, single=True):\n    # Load raw dataset\n    data = load_st_dataset(args.dataset)  # (timestamps, num_nodes, 3_channels)\n    \n    # Split data\n    if args.test_ratio > 1:\n        data_train, data_val, data_test = split_data_by_days(data, args.val_ratio, args.test_ratio)\n    else:\n        data_train, data_val, data_test = split_data_by_ratio(data, args.val_ratio, args.test_ratio)\n    \n    # Add sliding windows\n    x_tra, y_tra = Add_Window_Horizon(data_train, args.lag, args.horizon, single)\n    x_val, y_val = Add_Window_Horizon(data_val, args.lag, args.horizon, single)\n    x_test, y_test = Add_Window_Horizon(data_test, args.lag, args.horizon, single)\n    \n    # Normalize dataset\n    _, scaler_data, scaler_day, scaler_week = normalize_dataset(data_train, normalizer, args.column_wise)\n    \n    # Apply normalization separately to each channel\n    x_tra_data = scaler_data.transform(x_tra[:, :, :, 0:1])\n    x_tra_day = scaler_day.transform(x_tra[:, :, :, 1:2])\n    x_tra_week = scaler_week.transform(x_tra[:, :, :, 2:3])\n    x_tra = np.concatenate([x_tra_data, x_tra_day, x_tra_week], axis=-1)\n    \n    # Similar for val and test sets...\n    \n    # Create dataloaders\n    train_dataloader = data_loader(x_tra, y_tra, args.batch_size, shuffle=True, drop_last=False)\n    val_dataloader = data_loader(x_val, y_val, args.batch_size, shuffle=False, drop_last=False)\n    test_dataloader = data_loader(x_test, y_test, args.batch_size, shuffle=False, drop_last=False)\n    \n    return train_dataloader, val_dataloader, test_dataloader, scaler_data, scaler_day, scaler_week\n```\n\n## 6. Data Normalization\n\n**File**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST/lib/dataloader.py` (lines 29-68)\n\n```python\nelif normalizer == \'std\':\n    if column_wise:\n        mean = data.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n        std = data.std(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n        scaler = StandardScaler(mean, std)\n        data[:, :, 0:1] = scaler.transform(data[:, :, 0:1])\n    else:\n        # Separate scalers for each channel\n        data_ori = data[:, :, 0:1]  # Traffic flow\n        data_day = data[:, :, 1:2]  # Day feature\n        data_week = data[:, :, 2:3] # Week feature\n        \n        mean_data = data_ori.mean()\n        std_data = data_ori.std()\n        mean_day = data_day.mean()\n        std_day = data_day.std()\n        mean_week = data_week.mean()\n        std_week = data_week.std()\n        \n        scaler_data = StandardScaler(mean_data, std_data)\n        data_ori = scaler_data.transform(data_ori)\n        scaler_day = StandardScaler(mean_day, std_day)\n        data_day = scaler_day.transform(data_day)\n        scaler_week = StandardScaler(mean_week, std_week)\n        data_week = scaler_week.transform(data_week)\n        \n        data = np.concatenate([data_ori, data_day, data_week], axis=-1)\n```\n\n## 7. Dataset Loading\n\n**File**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST/lib/load_dataset.py` (lines 4-111)\n\n```python\ndef load_st_dataset(dataset):\n    # Load traffic flow data\n    if dataset == \'PEMS04\':\n        data_path = os.path.join(\'../PEMS_data/PEMS04/PEMS04.npz\')\n        data = np.load(data_path)[\'data\'][:, :, 0]  # Extract flow channel\n        \n        # Generate temporal features\n        day_data = np.zeros_like(data)\n        week_data = np.zeros_like(data)\n        day_init = 0\n        week_init = 0\n        \n        for index in range(data.shape[0]):\n            if (index) % (288 * 7) == 0:\n                week_init = 0\n            if (index) % 288 == 0:\n                day_init = 0\n            if (index) % 288 == 0:\n                week_init = week_init + 1\n            day_init = day_init + 1\n            day_data[index:index + 1, :] = day_init\n            week_data[index:index + 1, :] = week_init\n    \n    # Expand and concatenate channels\n    if len(data.shape) == 2:\n        data = np.expand_dims(data, axis=-1)\n        day_data = np.expand_dims(day_data, axis=-1)\n        week_data = np.expand_dims(week_data, axis=-1)\n        data = np.concatenate([data, day_data, week_data], axis=-1)\n    \n    return data  # (timestamps, num_nodes, 3_channels)\n```\n\n## 8. Configuration File\n\n**File**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST/model/PEMS04_MTGNN.conf`\n\n```ini\n[data]\nnum_nodes = 307\nlag = 12\nhorizon = 12\nval_ratio = 0.2\ntest_ratio = 0.2\ntod = False\nnormalizer = std\ncolumn_wise = False\ndefault_graph = True\n\n[model]\ninput_dim = 1\noutput_dim = 1\ninput_window = 12\noutput_window = 12\n\ngcn_true = True\nbuildA_true = True\ngcn_depth = 2\ndropout = 0.3\nsubgraph_size = 20\nnode_dim = 40\ndilation_exponential = 1\nconv_channels = 32\nresidual_channels = 32\nskip_channels = 64\nend_channels = 128\nlayers = 3\npropalpha = 0.05\ntanhalpha = 3\nlayer_norm_affline = True\nuse_curriculum_learning = True\ntask_level = 0\n\n[train]\nloss_func = mask_mae\nseed = 52\nbatch_size = 32\nepochs = 100\nlr_init = 0.003\nlr_decay = True\nlr_decay_rate = 0.3\nlr_decay_step = 25,45,60,75\nearly_stop = True\nearly_stop_patience = 15\ngrad_norm = True\nmax_grad_norm = 5\nreal_value = False\n```\n\n## 9. Graph Construction\n\n**File**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST/model/Teacher.py` (lines 155-193)\n\n```python\nclass GraphConstructor(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, nnodes, k, dim, device, alpha=3, static_feat=None):\n        super(GraphConstructor, self).__init__()\n        self.nnodes = nnodes\n        \n        if static_feat is not None:\n            xd = static_feat.shape[1]\n            self.lin1 = nn.Linear(xd, dim)\n            self.lin2 = nn.Linear(xd, dim)\n        else:\n            self.emb1 = nn.Embedding(nnodes, dim)\n            self.emb2 = nn.Embedding(nnodes, dim)\n            self.lin1 = nn.Linear(dim, dim)\n            self.lin2 = nn.Linear(dim, dim)\n        \n        self.device = device\n        self.k = k\n        self.dim = dim\n        self.alpha = alpha\n        self.static_feat = static_feat\n    \n    def forward(self, idx):\n        if self.static_feat is None:\n            nodevec1 = self.emb1(idx)\n            nodevec2 = self.emb2(idx)\n        else:\n            nodevec1 = self.static_feat[idx, :]\n            nodevec2 = nodevec1\n        \n        nodevec1 = torch.tanh(self.alpha * self.lin1(nodevec1))\n        nodevec2 = torch.tanh(self.alpha * self.lin2(nodevec2))\n        \n        # Compute affinity matrix\n        a = torch.mm(nodevec1, nodevec2.transpose(1, 0)) - torch.mm(nodevec2, nodevec1.transpose(1, 0))\n        adj = F.relu(torch.tanh(self.alpha * a))\n        \n        # Keep top-k neighbors\n        mask = torch.zeros(idx.size(0), idx.size(0)).to(self.device)\n        mask.fill_(float(\'0\'))\n        s1, t1 = adj.topk(self.k, 1)\n        mask.scatter_(1, t1, s1.fill_(1))\n        adj = adj * mask\n        \n        return adj\n```\n\n## 10. Evaluation Metrics\n\n**File**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST/lib/metrics.py` (lines 11-33)\n\n```python\ndef MAE_torch(pred, true, mask_value=None):\n    return torch.mean(torch.abs(true - pred))\n\ndef MSE_torch(pred, true, mask_value=None):\n    if mask_value != None:\n        mask = torch.gt(true, mask_value)\n        pred = torch.masked_select(pred, mask)\n        true = torch.masked_select(true, mask)\n    return torch.mean((pred - true) ** 2)\n\ndef RMSE_torch(pred, true, mask_value=None):\n    if mask_value != None:\n        mask = torch.gt(true, mask_value)\n        pred = torch.masked_select(pred, mask)\n        true = torch.masked_select(true, mask)\n    return torch.sqrt(torch.mean((pred - true) ** 2))\n\ndef MAPE_torch(pred, true, mask_value=None):\n    if mask_value != None:\n        mask = torch.gt(true, mask_value)\n        pred = torch.masked_select(pred, mask)\n        true = torch.masked_select(true, mask)\n    return torch.mean(torch.abs((pred - true) / true))\n```\n\n## 11. Training Entry Point\n\n**File**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST/model/Mains.py` (lines 1-50)\n\n```python\nimport torch\nimport numpy as np\nimport torch.nn as nn\nimport argparse\nimport configparser\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom model.teacher import STMLP as Network\nfrom model.BasicTrainer import Trainer\nfrom lib.TrainInits import init_seed\nfrom lib.dataloader import get_dataloader\nfrom lib.TrainInits import print_model_parameters\nfrom lib.metrics import MAE_torch\nfrom lib.pre_graph import get_adjacency_matrix\n\n# Configuration\nMode = \'train\'\nDEBUG = True\nDATASET = \'PEMS04\'\nDEVICE = \'cuda:0\'\nMODEL = \'MTGNN\'\n\n# Load configuration\nconfig_file = \'./{}_{}.conf\'.format(DATASET, MODEL)\nconfig = configparser.ConfigParser()\nconfig.read(config_file)\n\n# Define loss function wrapper\ndef scaler_mae_loss(scaler, mask_value):\n    def loss(preds, labels):\n        if scaler:\n            preds = scaler.inverse_transform(preds)\n            labels = scaler.inverse_transform(labels)\n        mae = MAE_torch(pred=preds, true=labels, mask_value=mask_value)\n        return mae\n    return loss\n\n# Initialize arguments\nargs = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\'arguments\')\nargs.add_argument(\'--dataset\', default=DATASET, type=str)\nargs.add_argument(\'--mode\', default=Mode, type=str)\nargs.add_argument(\'--device\', default=DEVICE, type=str)\nargs.add_argument(\'--debug\', default=DEBUG, type=eval)\nargs = args.parse_args()\n```\n\n---\n\n## Model Comparison: Teacher vs Student\n\n| Feature | Teacher | Student (STMLP) |\n|---------|---------|-----------------|\n| Spatial Processing | Full GCN | MLP only |\n| Parameters | Higher | Lower (distilled) |\n| Training | Standard supervised | With teacher guidance |\n| Graph Learning | Dynamic (GraphConstructor) | Disabled |\n| Computation | Heavier | Lighter |\n| Output Channels | Full resolution | Simplified |\n| Loss Function | MAE only | MAE + KL + Contrastive |\n\n## Key Insights\n\n1. **Efficiency through Distillation**: The student model achieves comparable performance to the teacher by learning from its representations, not just the final output.\n\n2. **Multi-objective Learning**: Three loss components:\n   - Primary task loss (MAE)\n   - Knowledge transfer (KL divergence)\n   - Feature alignment (Contrastive learning)\n\n3. **Temporal Feature Extraction**: Uses dilated convolutions with multiple kernel sizes to capture patterns at different time scales.\n\n4. **Spatial Modeling**: \n   - Teacher: Learns complex spatial relationships via GCN\n   - Student: Simplified via MLP, guided by teacher\'s spatial features\n\n5. **Pre-training Requirement**: Teacher model must be pre-trained on the same dataset before distillation can begin.\n\nEOF\ncat /home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/LIGHTST_CODE_SNIPPETS.md\n', 'description': 'Create code snippets document'}
[ERR] 2026-01-23 02:19:41 | INFO | Tool Bash called with {'command': 'cat > /home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/LIGHTST_SUMMARY.txt << \'EOF\'\n================================================================================\n                         LIGHTST REPOSITORY ANALYSIS\n                  Efficient Traffic Prediction through \n                        Spatio-Temporal Distillation\n================================================================================\n\nREPOSITORY INFORMATION\n================================================================================\nName:               LightST\nURL:                https://github.com/lizzyhku/TP\nCloned to:          /home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST\nConference:         AAAI 2025\nAuthors:            Zhang, Qianru; Gao, Xinyi; Wang, Haixin; Yiu, Siu Ming; Yin, Hongzhi\nPublication Year:   2025\n\nTASK DESCRIPTION\n================================================================================\nTask Type:          Traffic Flow Prediction (Time-series Forecasting)\nInput:              12 historical time steps (1 hour of 5-min intervals) of traffic flow\nOutput:             12 future time steps (1 hour of 5-min intervals) prediction\nFramework:          PyTorch\nPython Version:     3.9.13\nPyTorch Version:    1.12.1\nEvaluation Metrics: MAE, RMSE, MAPE\n\nCORE CONCEPT\n================================================================================\nLightST employs Knowledge Distillation to create an efficient traffic prediction model:\n- Teacher Model:    Complex MTGNN-based architecture with Graph Convolutional Networks (GCN)\n- Student Model:    Lightweight STMLP with only Multi-Layer Perceptrons (MLP) for spatial processing\n- Training:         Student learns from both ground truth (MAE loss) and teacher guidance (KL + Contrastive)\n- Result:           Significant parameter reduction while maintaining performance\n\nKEY INSIGHT: By distilling knowledge from a complex teacher, the lightweight student \nachieves comparable accuracy with much lower computational cost, enabling efficient \ndeployment for real-time traffic prediction.\n\nFILE STRUCTURE\n================================================================================\n\n/repos/LightST/\n├── model/\n│   ├── Teacher.py              - Teacher (complex GCN) & STMLP (lightweight MLP) models\n│   ├── Mains.py                - Training entry point\n│   ├── BasicTrainer.py          - Training loop with knowledge distillation\n│   ├── PEMS04_MTGNN.conf        - Configuration for PEMS04 dataset (307 nodes)\n│   ├── PEMS03_MTGNN.conf        - Configuration for PEMS03 dataset (358 nodes)\n│   ├── PEMS08_MTGNN.conf        - Configuration for PEMS08 dataset (170 nodes)\n│   └── SAVE/                    - Saved model checkpoints directory\n├── lib/\n│   ├── dataloader.py            - Data loading and preprocessing\n│   ├── load_dataset.py          - Load NPZ traffic flow datasets\n│   ├── metrics.py               - Evaluation metrics (MAE, RMSE, MAPE, etc.)\n│   ├── normalization.py         - Data normalization (std, min-max, etc.)\n│   ├── TrainInits.py            - Training initialization utilities\n│   ├── pre_graph.py             - Adjacency matrix generation from distance\n│   ├── add_window.py            - Sliding window generation\n│   └── logger.py                - Logging utilities\n├── PEMS_data/                   - Traffic dataset directory\n└── README.md                    - Documentation\n\nMODEL CLASSES\n================================================================================\n\n1. STMLP (Lightweight Student Model)\n   Location:    Teacher.py, lines 547-747\n   Inputs:      (batch_size, input_window, num_nodes, feature_dim)\n   Outputs:     (batch_size, output_window, num_nodes, 1)\n   Components:  \n     - DilatedInception: Temporal feature extraction (kernel sizes: 2,3,6,7)\n     - MLP Layers: 3 sequential MLP blocks for spatial processing\n     - Start/End Convolutions: Input/output projection layers\n     - Layer Normalization: Custom layer-wise normalization\n   \n   Key Feature: Uses only MLP for spatial processing (no GCN) - makes it lightweight\n\n2. Teacher (Complex Model with GCN)\n   Location:    Teacher.py, lines 337-546\n   Inputs:      Same as STMLP\n   Outputs:     Same as STMLP\n   Components:\n     - DilatedInception: Temporal feature extraction (same as student)\n     - MixProp: Mixed-scale graph propagation layers\n     - GraphConstructor: Learns adaptive adjacency matrices\n     - GCN Layers: Full spatial feature extraction via graph convolutions\n   \n   Key Feature: Uses full GCN for rich spatial modeling\n\n3. GraphConstructor\n   Location:    Teacher.py, lines 155-193\n   Purpose:     Learns adaptive spatial adjacency matrix\n   Features:    Top-k sparsification (k=20), learnable embeddings\n\nCONFIGURATION PARAMETERS\n================================================================================\n\nData Configuration:\n  num_nodes:         307/170/358/883 (depends on dataset)\n  lag:               12 (input window length)\n  horizon:           12 (output window length)\n  val_ratio:         0.2 (20% for validation)\n  test_ratio:        0.2 (20% for test)\n  normalizer:        \'std\' (standard normalization)\n\nModel Configuration:\n  input_dim:         1 (single traffic flow channel)\n  output_dim:        1\n  input_window:      12\n  output_window:     12\n  gcn_true:          True (use GCN in teacher)\n  buildA_true:       True (learn adjacency in teacher)\n  gcn_depth:         2\n  dropout:           0.3\n  subgraph_size:     20\n  node_dim:          40\n  conv_channels:     32\n  residual_channels: 32\n  skip_channels:     64\n  end_channels:      128\n  layers:            3\n\nTraining Configuration:\n  batch_size:        32 (PEMS04/08/03), 64 (PEMS07)\n  epochs:            100\n  lr_init:           0.003\n  lr_decay:          True (at epochs 25, 45, 60, 75)\n  lr_decay_rate:     0.3\n  early_stop:        True (patience=15)\n  grad_norm:         True (max_grad=5)\n  loss_func:         \'mask_mae\'\n\nTRAINING PIPELINE\n================================================================================\n\nStep 1: Data Preparation\n  - Load NPZ traffic flow datasets\n  - Generate temporal features (day-of-day, week-of-week)\n  - Split: 80% train, 10% val, 10% test\n  - Add sliding windows (lag=12, horizon=12)\n  - Normalize each channel separately\n\nStep 2: Model Initialization\n  - Create STMLP (student) model\n  - Load pre-trained Teacher model checkpoint\n    Location: ./SAVE/PEMS04/best_model.pth\n\nStep 3: Knowledge Distillation Training Loop (trainS method)\n  For each epoch:\n    1. Student forward:     (X) -> student_output, distill_features\n    2. Teacher forward:     (X) -> teacher_output, teacher_features (no_grad)\n    3. Compute loss:\n       - MAE(student_output, target)\n       - KL_divergence(student, teacher) * weight=10\n       - Spatial_contrastive_loss * weight=1\n       - Temporal_contrastive_loss (optional)\n    4. Backward + Gradient clipping (max_norm=5)\n    5. Validation (without teacher)\n    6. Early stopping if no improvement for 15 epochs\n\nStep 4: Model Checkpointing\n  - Best model: ./SAVE/<DATASET>/best_modelstudent.pth\n  - Test evaluation on held-out test set\n\nLOSS FUNCTIONS\n================================================================================\n\n1. Primary Prediction Loss (MAE)\n   loss_main = MAE(student_output, target)\n\n2. Knowledge Transfer Loss (KL Divergence)\n   kl_loss = KL_divergence(student_logits, teacher_logits)\n   weight: 10x\n\n3. Spatial Contrastive Loss (loss_cls)\n   - Normalizes features to unit norm\n   - Computes temperature-scaled cosine similarity\n   - Minimizes: -log(pos / (pos + neg))\n   - weight: 1x\n\n4. Temporal Contrastive Loss (loss_clt)\n   - Similar to spatial but applied to temporal features\n   - Currently not used in final loss (commented out)\n\nCombined Loss:\n  loss_total = loss_main + 10*kl_loss + 1*spatial_contrastive\n\nDATA FORMAT\n================================================================================\n\nInput Data:\n  Shape:            (num_timestamps, num_nodes, 3_channels)\n  Channel 0:        Traffic flow (vehicles per interval)\n  Channel 1:        Day-of-day index (0-287 for 5-min intervals)\n  Channel 2:        Week-of-week index (0-7)\n  Normalization:    Standard (per-channel mean/std from training set)\n\nSupported Datasets:\n  - PEMS04:   307 nodes, California highway sensors\n  - PEMS08:   170 nodes, California highway sensors\n  - PEMS03:   358 nodes, California highway sensors\n  - PEMS07:   883 nodes, California highway sensors\n  - PeMSBAY:  325 nodes, San Francisco Bay Area sensors\n\nData Availability:\n  Google Drive: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/146BOfs03ljP1OrWnVzdoleuywzCTpS69?usp=sharing\n\nRUNNING THE CODE\n================================================================================\n\nBasic command:\n  python Mains.py --data <DATASET>\n\nExamples:\n  python Mains.py --data PEMS04\n  python Mains.py --data PEMS08\n  python Mains.py --data PEMS03\n  python Mains.py --data PEMS07\n  python Mains.py --data PeMSBAY\n\nOutput:\n  - Training logs to console\n  - Model checkpoint: ./model/SAVE/<DATASET>/best_modelstudent.pth\n  - Test metrics: MAE, RMSE, MAPE\n\nEVALUATION METRICS\n================================================================================\n\nImplementation Location: lib/metrics.py\n\nMetrics Implemented:\n  - MAE (Mean Absolute Error)\n  - MSE (Mean Squared Error)\n  - RMSE (Root Mean Squared Error)\n  - MAPE (Mean Absolute Percentage Error)\n  - RRSE (Relative Root Squared Error)\n  - CORR (Correlation)\n\nFeatures:\n  - Mask-based filtering (removes zero/invalid values)\n  - PyTorch GPU-accelerated computation\n  - Support for N-dimensional tensor inputs\n\nARCHITECTURAL INNOVATIONS\n================================================================================\n\n1. Efficient Student-Teacher Distillation\n   - Teacher: Full MTGNN-based model\n   - Student: Lightweight MLP-based model\n   - Knowledge transfer via multiple loss components\n\n2. Multi-Level Knowledge Transfer\n   - Output-level: Direct prediction matching\n   - Intermediate-level: Feature alignment via contrastive learning\n   - Two separate contrastive losses for spatial and temporal features\n\n3. Dynamic Graph Learning (Teacher only)\n   - GraphConstructor learns adaptive adjacency matrices\n   - Top-k sparsification for efficiency\n   - Learnable node embeddings\n\n4. Dilated Temporal Convolutions\n   - Multiple kernel sizes (2, 3, 6, 7)\n   - Captures multi-scale temporal patterns\n   - Dilations for expanded receptive field\n\n5. Residual Connections\n   - Skip connections for gradient flow\n   - Residual connections within each layer\n   - Multi-level skip aggregation\n\nDEPENDENCIES\n================================================================================\n\nCore:\n  - PyTorch 1.12.1\n  - NumPy\n\nStandard Library:\n  - configparser (config file parsing)\n  - argparse (command-line arguments)\n  - torch.nn, torch.nn.functional\n  - os, sys, time, logging\n\nNo External Packages:\n  - No requirements.txt file\n  - Uses only PyTorch and NumPy\n\nMIGRATION CONSIDERATIONS FOR LIBCITY\n================================================================================\n\nStrengths:\n  1. Clear separation of teacher/student models\n  2. Well-structured data loading pipeline\n  3. Standard PyTorch components (no custom ops)\n  4. Clean configuration system\n  5. Modular loss functions\n\nChallenges:\n  1. Teacher model must be pre-trained before student training\n  2. Knowledge distillation requires careful weight tuning\n  3. Contrastive loss functions are custom implementations\n  4. Graph construction requires adjacency matrix input\n  5. Multiple output formats from models (3 outputs each)\n\nKey Files to Integrate:\n  - STMLP class (lightweight student for deployment)\n  - Knowledge distillation training loop\n  - Data loading and preprocessing pipeline\n  - Custom contrastive loss functions\n  - Metrics evaluation utilities\n\nConfiguration Parameters to Expose:\n  - Distillation loss weight (currently 10x)\n  - Contrastive loss weight (currently 1x)\n  - Temperature for contrastive learning (0.05)\n  - Teacher model checkpoint path\n  - Graph construction parameters (k, node_dim, etc.)\n  - Normalization strategy options\n\nRESEARCH PAPER REFERENCE\n================================================================================\n\nCitation:\n  @inproceedings{zhang2025efficient,\n    title={Efficient traffic prediction through spatio-temporal distillation},\n    author={Zhang, Qianru and Gao, Xinyi and Wang, Haixin and Yiu, Siu Ming and Yin, Hongzhi},\n    booktitle={Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence},\n    volume={39},\n    number={1},\n    pages={1093--1101},\n    year={2025}\n  }\n\nRelated Work:\n  - MTGNN: https://github.com/nnzhan/MTGNN\n  - Paper: "Connecting the Dots: Multivariate Time Series Forecasting with Graph Neural Networks"\n\n================================================================================\nAnalysis Generated: 2026-01-23\nStatus: Ready for LibCity Migration\n================================================================================\nEOF\ncat /home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/LIGHTST_SUMMARY.txt\n', 'description': 'Create comprehensive summary document'}
