hts\n3. Data has 3 channels: traffic flow, day-of-day, week-of-week\n4. Graph structure needed for teacher model\n5. Adjacency matrix computed from distance matrix\n\n### Configuration Parameters (Key for Tuning)\n- Distillation loss weight: 10x (currently)\n- Contrastive loss weight: 1x (currently)\n- Temperature for contrastive learning: 0.05\n- Max gradient norm: 5\n- Learning rate: 0.003 with decay at epochs 25, 45, 60, 75\n\n---\n\n## Dataset Information\n\n### Format\n- Traffic data: NPZ files (NumPy compressed format)\n- Distance matrix: CSV files\n- Shape: (num_timestamps, num_nodes, channels)\n- Channels: [traffic_flow, day_index, week_index]\n- Normalization: Standard (per-channel from training set)\n\n### Availability\nGoogle Drive: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/146BOfs03ljP1OrWnVzdoleuywzCTpS69?usp=sharing\n\n### Usage\nProvides 80-10-10 split for train-val-test with sliding windows (lag=12, horizon=12)\n\n---\n\n## Paper Reference\n\n```bibtex\n@inproceedings{zhang2025efficient,\n  title={Efficient traffic prediction through spatio-temporal distillation},\n  author={Zhang, Qianru and Gao, Xinyi and Wang, Haixin and Yiu, Siu Ming and Yin, Hongzhi},\n  booktitle={Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence},\n  volume={39},\n  number={1},\n  pages={1093--1101},\n  year={2025}\n}\n```\n\nRelated Work: MTGNN (https://github.com/nnzhan/MTGNN)\n\n---\n\n## Repository Structure\n\n```\n/repos/LightST/\n├── model/\n│   ├── Teacher.py              # Main model implementations\n│   ├── Mains.py                # Training entry point\n│   ├── BasicTrainer.py          # Training loop with distillation\n│   ├── PEMS04_MTGNN.conf        # Dataset configurations\n│   ├── PEMS03_MTGNN.conf\n│   ├── PEMS08_MTGNN.conf\n│   └── SAVE/                    # Model checkpoints\n├── lib/\n│   ├── dataloader.py            # Data loading pipeline\n│   ├── load_dataset.py          # Dataset utilities\n│   ├── metrics.py               # Evaluation metrics\