[ERR] 2026-01-23 02:24:57 | INFO | Tool Write called with {'file_path': '/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/LIGHTST_ADAPTATION_DOCUMENTATION.md', 'content': '# LightST Model Adaptation Documentation\n\n## Overview\nThis document describes the adaptation of the LightST (STMLP) model from the original research repository to LibCity framework conventions.\n\n**Original Paper**: "Efficient traffic prediction through spatio-temporal distillation" (AAAI 2025)\n**Authors**: Zhang et al.\n**Original Repository**: https://github.com/lizzyhku/TP\n**Date Adapted**: 2026-01-23\n\n---\n\n## Model Information\n\n### Task Type\nTraffic flow prediction\n\n### Model Architecture\nLightST is a lightweight student model designed through knowledge distillation from a complex teacher network. The adapted version implements the STMLP (Student MLP) architecture without the distillation components.\n\n**Key Components**:\n1. **DilatedInception**: Multi-scale temporal convolution with kernel sizes [2, 3, 6, 7]\n2. **MLP Layers**: 3 sequential MLP blocks for spatial processing (replacing GCN)\n3. **Skip Connections**: Multi-level skip connections for gradient flow\n4. **Layer Normalization**: Custom layer norm with node indexing\n\n---\n\n## File Locations\n\n### Source Files (Original Repository)\n- **Main Model**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST/model/Teacher.py`\n  - STMLP class (lines 547-747)\n  - DilatedInception class (lines 136-152)\n  - LayerNorm class (lines 300-334)\n\n### Target Files (LibCity)\n- **Model Implementation**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_flow_prediction/LightST.py`\n- **Configuration**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/LightST.json`\n- **Registration**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_flow_prediction/__init__.py`\n\n---\n\n## Key Adaptations\n\n### 1. Base Class Inheritance\n**Original**:\n```python\nclass STMLP(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, args):\n```\n\n**Adapted**:\n```python\nclass LightST(AbstractTrafficStateModel):\n    def __init__(self, config, data_feature):\n```\n\n**Changes**:\n- Inherits from `AbstractTrafficStateModel`\n- Constructor takes `config` dict and `data_feature` dict\n- Extracts num_nodes, feature_dim from data_feature\n\n### 2. Data Format Handling\n**Original**:\n```python\ndef forward(self, source, idx=None):\n    inputs = source\n    inputs = inputs.transpose(1, 3)  # [B, 1, N, T]\n```\n\n**Adapted**:\n```python\ndef forward(self, batch):\n    inputs = batch[\'X\']  # [B, T, N, C]\n    inputs = inputs.transpose(1, 3)  # [B, C, N, T]\n```\n\n**Changes**:\n- Input is a batch dictionary with key \'X\'\n- LibCity format: [batch, time, nodes, features]\n- Transpose to [batch, channels, nodes, time] for convolution\n\n### 3. Output Format\n**Original**:\n```python\nreturn x, x_, x  # Returns 3 outputs for distillation\n```\n\n**Adapted**:\n```python\nx = x.transpose(1, 3).transpose(1, 2)  # [B, T, N, C]\nreturn x  # Single output tensor\n```\n\n**Changes**:\n- Removed distillation outputs (x_, intermediate features)\n- Transpose output back to LibCity format [B, T, N, C]\n- Returns only the prediction tensor\n\n### 4. Loss Calculation\n**Original**:\n```python\n# Loss computed in external trainer with teacher outputs\nloss = MAE + 10*KL_divergence + contrastive_loss\n```\n\n**Adapted**:\n```python\ndef calculate_loss(self, batch):\n    y_true = batch[\'y\']\n    y_predicted = self.predict(batch)\n    y_true = self._scaler.inverse_transform(y_true[..., :self.output_dim])\n    y_predicted = self._scaler.inverse_transform(y_predicted[..., :self.output_dim])\n    return loss.masked_mae_torch(y_predicted, y_true, 0)\n```\n\n**Changes**:\n- Implemented standard supervised loss (no distillation)\n- Uses LibCity\'s masked MAE loss\n- Handles scaler inverse transform automatically\n\n### 5. Graph/Adjacency Matrix\n**Original**:\n```python\n# Uses GraphConstructor to build adaptive adjacency\nself.gc = GraphConstructor(self.num_nodes, ...)\nadp = self.gc(self.idx)  # In forward pass\n```\n\n**Adapted**:\n```python\n# Removed graph construction completely\n# Model uses only MLP layers (no GCN), so no adjacency needed\n```\n\n**Changes**:\n- Removed all graph construction code\n- The STMLP variant doesn\'t use GCN, only MLP\n- Simplifies dependencies and makes model lighter\n\n### 6. Device Handling\n**Original**:\n```python\nself.device = args.device\nself.idx = torch.arange(self.num_nodes).to(self.device)\n```\n\n**Adapted**:\n```python\nself.device = config.get(\'device\', torch.device(\'cpu\'))\nself.idx = torch.arange(self.num_nodes).to(self.device)\n```\n\n**Changes**:\n- Device extracted from config with default fallback\n- Node indices moved to correct device\n\n---\n\n## Configuration Parameters\n\n### Model Architecture\n```json\n{\n  "dropout": 0.3,                    // Dropout rate\n  "layers": 3,                       // Number of temporal layers\n  "dilation_exponential": 1,         // Dilation growth (1 = linear)\n  "residual_channels": 32,           // Residual convolution channels\n  "conv_channels": 32,               // Temporal convolution channels\n  "skip_channels": 64,               // Skip connection channels\n  "end_channels": 128,               // Output layer channels\n  "layer_norm_affline": true         // Enable learnable norm params\n}\n```\n\n### Training Parameters\n```json\n{\n  "max_epoch": 100,\n  "learner": "adam",\n  "learning_rate": 0.003,\n  "lr_decay": true,\n  "lr_decay_ratio": 0.3,\n  "step_size": 25,\n  "clip_grad_norm": true,\n  "max_grad_norm": 5,\n  "use_early_stop": true,\n  "patience": 15\n}\n```\n\n### Data Parameters\n```json\n{\n  "scaler": "standard",              // Normalization method\n  "add_time_in_day": false,          // Temporal features\n  "add_day_in_week": false\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Model Workflow\n\n### Input Shape\n`[batch_size, input_window, num_nodes, feature_dim]`\n\nExample: `[32, 12, 307, 1]` for PEMS04\n\n### Processing Steps\n1. **Transpose**: [B, T, N, C] → [B, C, N, T]\n2. **Padding**: If input_window < receptive_field\n3. **Start Conv**: [B, C, N, T] → [B, residual_channels, N, T]\n4. **For each layer**:\n   - Gated temporal convolution (DilatedInception)\n   - Skip connection\n   - MLP spatial processing\n   - Residual addition\n   - Layer normalization\n5. **End Conv**: → [B, output_window, N, 1]\n6. **Transpose**: → [B, T, N, C]\n\n### Output Shape\n`[batch_size, output_window, num_nodes, output_dim]`\n\nExample: `[32, 12, 307, 1]`\n\n---\n\n## Removed Components\n\nThe following components from the original implementation were removed as they are not needed for standard LibCity training:\n\n### 1. Knowledge Distillation\n- Teacher model loading\n- KL divergence loss\n- Intermediate feature outputs (x_, ttout, ssout)\n\n### 2. Contrastive Learning\n- Spatial-temporal contrastive losses\n- Temperature-scaled similarity computation\n\n### 3. Graph Construction\n- GraphConstructor class\n- Adaptive adjacency matrix learning\n- Pre-defined adjacency matrix handling\n- All GCN-related code (MixProp, NConv)\n\n### 4. Transformer Components\n- TransformerEncoder (was optional/commented in original)\n- Self-attention mechanisms\n\n---\n\n## Preserved Components\n\n### 1. Core Architecture\n- **DilatedInception**: Multi-scale temporal convolution\n- **LayerNorm**: Custom normalization with indexing\n- **MLP Layers**: 3 sequential MLPs for spatial processing\n- **Skip Connections**: Multi-level skip paths\n\n### 2. Temporal Processing\n- Receptive field calculation\n- Dilation factor progression\n- Gated convolution (tanh × sigmoid)\n\n### 3. Residual Learning\n- Residual connections at each layer\n- Skip connections from input and intermediate layers\n\n---\n\n## Testing and Validation\n\n### Import Test\n```python\nfrom libcity.model.traffic_flow_prediction import LightST\nprint("LightST imported successfully")\n```\n\n### Model Instantiation Test\n```python\nconfig = {\n    \'input_window\': 12,\n    \'output_window\': 12,\n    \'dropout\': 0.3,\n    \'layers\': 3,\n    \'residual_channels\': 32,\n    \'conv_channels\': 32,\n    \'skip_channels\': 64,\n    \'end_channels\': 128,\n}\n\ndata_feature = {\n    \'num_nodes\': 307,\n    \'feature_dim\': 1,\n    \'output_dim\': 1,\n    \'scaler\': None\n}\n\nmodel = LightST(config, data_feature)\n```\n\n### Forward Pass Test\n```python\nbatch = {\n    \'X\': torch.randn(32, 12, 307, 1),\n    \'y\': torch.randn(32, 12, 307, 1)\n}\n\noutput = model(batch)\nloss = model.calculate_loss(batch)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Known Limitations\n\n### 1. Fixed Temporal Dimensions\nThe MLP layers are hardcoded for specific temporal dimensions (13, 7, 1) which corresponds to:\n- Input window: 12\n- Layers: 3\n- Dilation pattern with kernel size 7\n\n**Implication**: Changing `input_window` or `layers` may require adjusting MLP dimensions.\n\n**Potential Fix**: Make MLP dimensions dynamic based on calculated temporal sizes.\n\n### 2. Single Output Dimension\nCurrent implementation assumes `output_dim = 1` (predicting only flow).\n\n**Implication**: Multi-dimensional outputs would require modifications.\n\n### 3. No Graph Structure\nThe model doesn\'t use any graph/adjacency information, relying only on temporal and MLP-based spatial processing.\n\n**Implication**: May underperform compared to graph-based models on datasets with strong spatial correlations.\n\n---\n\n## Performance Expectations\n\n### Original Paper Results (PEMS04)\n- **STMLP Student Model**:\n  - MAE: ~21.5\n  - RMSE: ~34.8\n  - MAPE: ~14.2%\n\n- **Efficiency**:\n  - Significantly fewer parameters than teacher\n  - Faster inference time\n  - Maintained competitive accuracy through distillation\n\n### Expected LibCity Results\n- Slightly lower accuracy than original (no distillation)\n- Faster training (no teacher model needed)\n- Similar inference speed\n- Good baseline for lightweight traffic prediction\n\n---\n\n## Usage in LibCity\n\n### Training Command\n```bash\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred \\\n                    --model LightST \\\n                    --dataset PEMS04 \\\n                    --config_file LightST.json\n```\n\n### Custom Configuration\n```python\n# In experiment config\n{\n    "model": "LightST",\n    "dataset": "PEMS04",\n    "input_window": 12,\n    "output_window": 12,\n    "dropout": 0.3,\n    "learning_rate": 0.003\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Future Enhancements\n\n### 1. Dynamic MLP Dimensions\nCalculate MLP input/output dimensions based on temporal evolution through layers.\n\n### 2. Optional Graph Support\nAdd optional GCN layers (from original Teacher model) that can be enabled via config.\n\n### 3. Knowledge Distillation Support\nImplement optional distillation training within LibCity framework:\n- Load pre-trained teacher model\n- Add distillation loss as auxiliary objective\n- Support both standalone and distillation modes\n\n### 4. Multi-Output Support\nExtend to predict multiple traffic features (flow, speed, occupancy).\n\n---\n\n## References\n\n### Original Paper\n```bibtex\n@inproceedings{zhang2025efficient,\n  title={Efficient traffic prediction through spatio-temporal distillation},\n  author={Zhang, Qianru and Gao, Xinyi and Wang, Haixin and Yiu, Siu Ming and Yin, Hongzhi},\n  booktitle={Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence},\n  volume={39},\n  number={1},\n  pages={1093--1101},\n  year={2025}\n}\n```\n\n### Original Repository\n- GitHub: https://github.com/lizzyhku/TP\n- Cloned to: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST`\n\n### LibCity Framework\n- Documentation: https://bigscity-libcity-docs.readthedocs.io/\n- Repository: https://github.com/LibCity/Bigscity-LibCity\n\n---\n\n## Contact and Maintenance\n\n**Adapter**: Model Adaptation Agent\n**Date**: 2026-01-23\n**LibCity Version**: Compatible with current main branch\