ata PEMS08\npython Mains.py --data PEMS03\npython Mains.py --data PEMS07\npython Mains.py --data PEMSBAY\n```\n\n### Training Process (trainS method)\n1. Initialize student model (STMLP)\n2. Load pre-trained teacher model from checkpoint\n3. For each epoch:\n   - Train student with teacher supervision\n   - Compute loss: MAE + KL divergence + contrastive loss\n   - Validate on validation set\n   - Early stopping if no improvement\n4. Save best student model\n5. Evaluate on test set\n\n### Model Classes Used\n- **Student**: `STMLP` (lightweight with MLP)\n- **Teacher**: `Teacher` (full model with GCN)\n- **Trainer**: `Trainer` class handles orchestration\n\n---\n\n## Key Insights for Migration\n\n1. **Model Classes**:\n   - Core prediction: `STMLP` (student model - main target)\n   - Reference: `Teacher` (teacher model - for distillation)\n   - Both inherit from `nn.Module`\n\n2. **Input/Output Specs**:\n   - Input: `(batch, 12, num_nodes, 1)` - 12 time steps, variable nodes, 1 feature\n   - Output: `(batch, 12, num_nodes, 1)` - 12 time steps prediction\n   - Also outputs: intermediate features for distillation\n\n3. **Graph Information**:\n   - Precomputed adjacency matrix from distance CSV files\n   - Can be optionally built adaptively\n\n4. **Special Features**:\n   - Knowledge distillation framework\n   - Temporal contrastive learning\n   - Spatial-temporal feature matching\n   - Dynamic graph construction capability\n\n5. **Computational Efficiency**:\n   - Student model uses MLP instead of GCN\n   - Reduces parameters and inference time significantly\n   - Still achieves competitive performance through distillation\n\nEOF\ncat /tmp/lightst_analysis.md\n", 'description': 'Create comprehensive analysis report'}
