e = 15\n```\n\n---\n\n## Dependencies\n\n### Required\n- Python: 3.9.13\n- PyTorch: 1.12.1\n- NumPy\n- configparser (standard library)\n- argparse (standard library)\n\n### Optional (for data download)\n- Google Drive API or manual download from provided link\n\n---\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Training\n```bash\ncd /home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST/model\npython Mains.py --data PEMS04\npython Mains.py --data PEMS08\npython Mains.py --data PEMS03\npython Mains.py --data PEMS07\npython Mains.py --data PEMSBAY\n```\n\n### Testing\n```bash\npython Mains.py --data PEMS04 --mode test\n```\n\n### Configuration\nModify corresponding `.conf` file:\n- `PEMS04_MTGNN.conf` for PEMS04 dataset\n- `PEMS03_MTGNN.conf` for PEMS03 dataset\n- `PEMS08_MTGNN.conf` for PEMS08 dataset\n\n---\n\n## Migration Target: STMLP Model\n\nThe **STMLP class** in `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST/model/Teacher.py` (lines 547-747) is the primary target for migration to LibCity.\n\n### Key Characteristics\n1. **Lightweight Design**: Uses MLPs instead of GCNs for spatial modeling\n2. **Efficient**: Reduced parameters while maintaining competitive performance\n3. **Flexible**: Can work with or without graph information\n4. **Scalable**: Supports variable number of nodes\n5. **Well-tested**: Validated on multiple PEMS datasets\n\n### Critical Implementation Details\n- Input transpose: `(batch, window, nodes, dim) → (batch, dim, nodes, window)`\n- Output transpose: `(batch, dim, nodes, window) → (batch, window, nodes, dim)`\n- Multi-output: Returns prediction + intermediate features for distillation\n- Graph optional: Can use predefined or learnable adjacency matrix\n- Temporal dilation: Uses dilated convolutions with kernels [2,3,6,7]\n- Normalization: Layer normalization applied after spatial processing\n\n---\n\n## Documentation Files Generated\n\n1. **LightST_MIGRATION_SUMMARY.md** (this file) - Complete overview\n2. **lightst_analysis.md** - Detailed technical analy