ectional edges with top-k filtering\n- Normalized adjacency matrices\n\n### 3. Trainer - BasicTrainer\n\n**File**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST/model/BasicTrainer.py`\n\n**Main Methods**:\n\n1. **train_epochs(epoch)** (lines 149-205)\n   - Knowledge distillation training\n   - Uses teacher and student models\n   - Multi-loss optimization\n\n2. **trainS()** (lines 267-323)\n   - Student model training pipeline\n   - Loads pre-trained teacher\n   - Implements early stopping\n   - Saves best model\n\n3. **train_epoch(epoch)** (lines 76-107)\n   - Standard supervised training (without distillation)\n\n4. **val_epoch(epoch, val_dataloader)** (lines 57-74)\n   - Validation evaluation\n\n5. **test(model, args, data_loader, scaler, logger)** (lines 336+)\n   - Test evaluation with metrics\n\n6. **loadTeacher(args)** (lines 48-56)\n   - Load pre-trained teacher model from checkpoint\n\n---\n\n## Knowledge Distillation Mechanism\n\n### Loss Functions\n\n```python\nTotal Loss = Task_Loss + 10*KL_Loss + 1*Contrastive_Loss\n\nComponents:\n1. Task Loss (MAE):\n   MAE(student_pred, ground_truth)\n\n2. KL Divergence Loss (10x weight):\n   KL(F.log_softmax(student_out), F.log_softmax(teacher_out))\n   \n3. Spatial-Temporal Contrastive Loss (1x weight):\n   - loss_cls(): Spatial contrastive loss\n   - loss_clt(): Temporal contrastive loss\n   - Uses temperature-scaled cosine similarity\n   - Weight by feature similarity\n```\n\n### Contrastive Learning\n\n**Temperature-scaled NT-Xent Loss**:\n```python\ndef loss_cls(x1, x2):\n    temperature = 0.05\n    x1_norm = normalize(x1)\n    x2_norm = normalize(x2)\n    weight = cosine_similarity(x1, x2)\n    \n    pos = exp(sum(x1*x2)*weight / temperature)\n    neg = exp(matmul(all_features, all_features.T) / temperature)\n    \n    loss = -log(pos / (pos + neg))\n```\n\n### Training Flow\n\n1. Student forward: `student_out, student_features = student(X)`\n2. Teacher forward (no_grad): `teacher_out, teacher_features = teacher(X)`\n3. Compute losses for all components\n4. Backprop through student only\n5. Update student parameters\n6. Log and validate\n\n---\n\n## Data Pipeline\n\n### Supported Datasets\n\n| Dataset | Nodes | Files |\n|---------|-------|-------|\n| PEMS04  | 307   | .npz  |\n| PEMS08  | 170   | .npz  |\n| PEMS03  | 358   | .npz  |\n| PEMS07  | 883   | .npz  |\n| PEMSBay | 325   | .npz  |\n\n### Data Format\n\n**Input NPZ Structure**:\n```\ndata.npz['data']: shape (time_steps, num_nodes, 1)\n# Feature 0: Traffic flow\n# Feature 1: Day-of-week (added during preprocessing)\n# Feature 2: Week-of-year (added during preprocessing)\n```\n\n### Preprocessing Steps\n\n1. **Load Raw Data** (`load_st_dataset()`)\n   - Load NPZ from `../PEMS_data/<DATASET>/`\n   - Extract first dimension (traffic flow)\n\n2. **Generate Temporal Features** (`load_st_dataset()`)\n   - Day-of-week: 0-287 per day (5-min intervals)\n   - Week-of-year: Encoded week number\n\n3. **Split Dataset** (`split_data_by_ratio()`)\n   - Train: 60% (default)\n   - Validation: 20% (default)\n   - Test: 20% (default)\n\n4. **Create Windows** (`Add_Window_Horizon()`)\n   - Input window: 12 timesteps\n   - Output window: 12 timesteps (horizon)\n   - Overlap: Sequential sliding\n\n5. **Normalize Data** (`normalize_dataset()`)\n   - Method: Standard normalization\n   - Computed per feature dimension\n   - Saved for inverse transformation\n\n6. **Create DataLoaders** (`get_dataloader()`)\n   - Batch size: 32-64\n   - Shuffle: True for training\n   - Drop last: False\n\n### Data Shapes\n\n```\nRaw: (T, N, 1) where T=time_steps, N=nodes\nAfter windowing: (S, 12, N, 1) where S=samples\nAfter augmentation: (S, 12, N, 3) with temporal features\nAfter batching: (B, 12, N, 3) where B=batch_size\nModel input: (B, 1, N, 12) after transpose\n```\n\n---\n\n## Configuration Files\n\n### PEMS04_MTGNN.conf Example\n\n**[data] Section**:\n- `num_nodes`: 307 (fixed per dataset)\n- `lag`: 12 (historical timesteps)\n- `horizon`: 12 (prediction steps)\n- `val_ratio`: 0.2 (validation split)\n- `test_ratio`: 0.2 (test split)\n- `normalizer`: std (standardization)\n- `column_wise`: False (global normalization)\n\n**[model] Section**:\n- `input_dim`: 1 (traffic flow)\n- `output_dim`: 1 (predicted flow)\n- `input_window`: 12 (must match lag)\n- `output_window`: 12 (must match horizon)\n- `gcn_true`: True (use graph convolutions)\n- `buildA_true`: True (learn adjacency matrix)\n- `dropout`: 0.3 (regularization)\n- `conv_channels`: 32\n- `residual_channels`: 32\n- `skip_channels`: 64\n- `end_channels`: 128\n- `layers`: 3 (number of dilated layers)\n\n**[train] Section**:\n- `loss_func`: mask_mae\n- `batch_size`: 32 (or 64 for PEMS7)\n- `epochs`: 100\n- `lr_init`: 0.003\n- `lr_decay`: True\n- `lr_decay_rate`: 0.3\n- `lr_decay_step`: 25,45,60,75\n- `early_stop`: True\n- `early_stop_patience`: 15\n\n---\n\n## Dependencies & Requirements\n\n### Framework Stack\n- **Python**: 3.9.13\n- **PyTorch**: 1.12.1\n- **CUDA**: Required for GPU training\n\n### Standard Libraries\n- `torch` - Neural network framework\n- `numpy` - Numerical computing\n- `configparser` - Configuration file handling\n- `argparse` - Command-line argument parsing\n- `time` - Timing utilities\n- `os` - File operations\n- `copy` - Model state copying\n- `torch.nn.functional` - Functional operations\n- `torch.optim` - Optimization\n\n### No External Dependencies Beyond PyTorch+NumPy\n\nThe repository is self-contained with all utilities implemented in Python.\n\n---\n\n## How to Run\n\n### Prerequisites\n1. Clone repository (already done)\n2. Download PEMS datasets to `./PEMS_data/<DATASET>/`\n3. Install PyTorch 1.12.1\n4. Ensure Python 3.9.13+\n\n### Training Command\n```bash\ncd /home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/LightST/model\npython Mains.py --data PEMS04\n```\n\n### Optional Arguments\n- `--mode`: 'train' or 'test' (default: train)\n- `--device`: GPU device ID (default: cuda:0)\n- `--debug`: Enable debug mode (default: True)\n