s Features\n1. **Lightweight**: Reduces GCN to MLP for efficiency\n2. **Flexible**: Works with or without graph information\n3. **Scalable**: Variable number of nodes\n4. **Proven**: AAAI 2025 publication\n\n### Recommended Adaptations\n1. Remove distillation if not needed\n2. Adapt configuration format to LibCity style\n3. Update data loader interface\n4. Create LibCity wrapper for model initialization\n5. Integrate with LibCity evaluation framework\n\n### Preserved Features\n- Input/output shapes\n- Temporal convolution architecture\n- Layer normalization\n- Residual connections\n- Skip connections\n\n---\n\n## Paper Information\n\n**Title**: Efficient Traffic Prediction Through Spatio-Temporal Distillation\n\n**Citation**:\n```bibtex\n@inproceedings{zhang2025efficient,\n  title={Efficient traffic prediction through spatio-temporal distillation},\n  author={Zhang, Qianru and Gao, Xinyi and Wang, Haixin and Yiu, Siu Ming and Yin, Hongzhi},\n  booktitle={Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence},\n  volume={39},\n  number={1},\n  pages={1093--1101},\n  year={2025}\n}\n```\n\n**Base Work**: MTGNN (Connecting the Dots, SIGKDD 2020)\n```bibtex\n@inproceedings{wu2020connecting,\n  title={Connecting the Dots: Multivariate Time Series Forecasting with Graph Neural Networks},\n  author={Wu, Zonghan and Pan, Shirui and Long, Guodong and Jiang, Jing and Chang, Xiaojun and Zhang, Chengqi},\n  booktitle={Proceedings of the 26th ACM SIGKDD International Conference on Knowledge Discovery & Data Mining},\n  year={2020}\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## File Reference Summary\n\n### Main Files (Must Read for Migration)\n1. `/repos/LightST/model/Teacher.py` - STMLP and Teacher classes\n2. `/repos/LightST/model/BasicTrainer.py` - Training logic\n3. `/repos/LightST/model/Mains.py` - Entry point and configuration\n4. `/repos/LightST/lib/dataloader.py` - Data loading pipeline\n\n### Supporting Files\n5. `/repos/LightST/lib/metrics.py` - Evaluation metrics\n6. `/repos/LightST/li